From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: trace passthrough measurement windows and correction ownership

Record immutable physical and compatibility averages, whole-window saturation,
observation identity and software delay-reset provenance. Keep existing error
accumulators, cached corrections, thresholds and output policy unchanged.
Aggregate engine mute/insert/drop requests and correlate player corrections
with the snapshot actually accepted by its legacy timestamp gate. Compare
value-based freshness with window identity without changing the decision.

Shared AudioEngine and VideoPlayer changes are necessary because these own the
measurements and corrections; AML consumers cannot reconstruct their windows
or correction provenance. This is diagnostic infrastructure, not a receiver
readiness contract or proof of audible synchronization. LOGAUDIO window records
are bounded to publication/reset events; declined clock corrections are logged
once per accepted snapshot. Requested burst duration is not hardware output.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

